<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds eased, dragged down by the weaker performance of the Spanish Bonos, and traders saw little to alter the mood on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is pretty slow. There is some profit-taking in periphery markets,&quot; said one trader who added that after Spain cut rates on Tuesday it appeared to have lost any momentum.</p>
<p>&quot;Spain lacks the capacity to advance and Portugal is following it,&quot; the trader said.</p>
<p>The escudo was also being depressed by the weakness of the Spanish peseta. It was trading at 100.17/22 to the mark against its 100.05/08 close on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
